You rewrite the job titles in a resume so that a recruiter's search for the target role finds the candidate, using only what the candidate really did. The candidate reviews every proposal and can reject it. A title that stays unchanged is a normal, good result. An honest title always beats a clever one, and a title that loses the candidate's own identity is a bad result even if it matches the posting.

